{"is_error":false,"duration_api_ms":82189,"num_turns":1,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"c46c4568-9b46-5b45-bf69-b2131339c345","total_cost_usd":0.687248,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":13340,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":8238,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":13340,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":8238,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":13340,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":13340},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":8458,"outputTokens":14,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.008528,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000,"canonicalModel":"claude-haiku-4-5","provider":"firstParty"},"claude-fable-5":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":8238,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":13340,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.67872,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"canonicalModel":"claude-fable-5","provider":"firstParty"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"reviewer_participant_id\": \"actor:v204h-reviewer-fable-01\", \"reviews\": [{\"case_id\": \"case:418f25ca12ef658137ff\", \"verdict\": \"demonstrated_issue\", \"bounded_statement\": \"The report's selected result asserts a fledging-success rate for 'the complete planned set of 48 kittiwake nest sites' while the rate itself (0.6500, 65.00 percent) is computed as 26 events over only the 40 retained post-screening nest sites; the 8 screened-out nest sites are absent from the denominator, so the retained-subset rate is presented as the rate for the complete planned domain that the task designates as the scientific target.\", \"root_cause\": \"workflow/analysis.py computes the selected rate as Fraction(events, retained) (the retained-subset denominator) but templates that value into report text that labels the scientific target and the rate's referent as the complete planned set of 48 nest sites, creating a mismatch between the claimed domain (48 planned units) and the computed exposure base (40 retained units).\", \"issue_class\": \"issue-class:retained-subset-for-complete-domain\", \"evidence_atoms\": [{\"description\": \"Task requires the reported rate's scientific target to be the complete planned set of observation units.\", \"observed_value\": \"complete planned set required\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"task.md\", \"start_line\": 1, \"end_line\": 1, \"quoted_text\": \"Report one occurrence rate whose scientific target is the complete planned set of observation units, using the planned-unit accounting supplied with this workflow.\"}]}, {\"description\": \"The selected result claims the rate applies to the complete planned set of 48 nest sites while the arithmetic shown uses the 40 retained nest sites as denominator (26/40 = 0.6500).\", \"observed_value\": \"0.6500 claimed for 48 planned units, computed over 40 retained units\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"results/report.md\", \"start_line\": 23, \"end_line\": 23, \"quoted_text\": \"[selected-result] Fledging success of the complete planned set of 48 kittiwake nest sites is 0.6500 fledged chicks per nest site (65.00 percent), computed as 26 fledging events over 40 nest sites.\"}]}, {\"description\": \"The scientific-target section explicitly states the selected rate is reported for the complete planned set of 48 sites.\", \"observed_value\": \"target = 48 planned sites\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"results/report.md\", \"start_line\": 5, \"end_line\": 8, \"quoted_text\": \"The scientific target of this analysis is the complete planned set of 48\\nkittiwake nest sites mapped on the Fulmar Head cliff transect before the 2025\\nbreeding season. The selected rate below is reported for that complete planned\\nset.\"}]}, {\"description\": \"The workflow source computes the selected rate with the retained-subset denominator, confirmed by its own comment.\", \"observed_value\": \"rate = Fraction(events, retained)\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"workflow/analysis.py\", \"start_line\": 54, \"end_line\": 55, \"quoted_text\": \"    # Selected rate: fledging events per retained nest site.\\n    rate = Fraction(events, retained)\"}]}, {\"description\": \"Unit accounting confirms 48 planned versus 40 retained, so the denominator mismatch is 8 units; I independently verified from inputs/data.csv that exactly 8 rows (N05, N11, N17, N23, N29, N34, N41, N46) have confirmed_visits_incubation < 3 and that 26 retained rows have fledged_chick = yes, so 26/40 = 0.65 and 26/48 = 0.5417.\", \"observed_value\": \"planned=48, retained=40, removed=8, events=26\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"results/report.md\", \"start_line\": 12, \"end_line\": 15, \"quoted_text\": \"- Planned nest sites: 48\\n- Retained after screening: 40\\n- Removed by screening: 8\\n- Fledging events (chick fledged) among retained nest sites: 26\"}]}], \"counterevidence_atoms\": [{\"description\": \"The report transparently discloses the screening rule and the retained/removed counts, and the selected-result sentence itself states the 26/40 computation, so a careful reader can detect the mismatch; this transparency could be argued to mitigate, but it does not change the explicit claim that 0.6500 is the rate for the complete planned set of 48.\", \"observed_value\": \"screening rule and counts disclosed\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"results/report.md\", \"start_line\": 17, \"end_line\": 19, \"quoted_text\": \"Prespecified screening rule: a planned nest site is retained only if it received\\nat least 3 confirmed observation visits during the incubation window. Nest sites\\nremoved by screening have no fledging outcome recorded.\"}]}], \"falsification_attempt\": \"I tried to defeat the verdict three ways. (1) Could 0.6500 legitimately be a complete-planned-set rate? No: 26/48 = 0.5417, so the reported 0.6500 is arithmetically only obtainable with the 40-unit retained denominator, which I verified against the raw CSV. (2) Could the report be read as claiming only a retained-subset rate? No: both the scientific-target section (lines 5-8) and the selected-result sentence (line 23) explicitly attach the rate to 'the complete planned set of 48 kittiwake nest sites'. (3) Could the disclosure of the 26/40 computation in the same sentence resolve the issue? No: the issue class concerns presenting a retained-subset statistic as the value for the complete domain, and the sentence does exactly that regardless of the disclosed arithmetic; there is also no protocol amendment or approved deviation (the report states none exists) that would redefine the target.\", \"cross_case_evidence_used\": false, \"unresolved_material_questions\": [], \"self_reported_confidence\": \"high\"}, {\"case_id\": \"case:63b01ef614ee3ea4e9d0\", \"verdict\": \"no_demonstrated_issue_within_scope\", \"bounded_statement\": null, \"root_cause\": null, \"issue_class\": null, \"evidence_atoms\": [{\"description\": \"Task requires the rate's scientific target to be the complete planned set, and the selected result uses all 48 planned nest sites as the denominator (26/48 = 0.5417), matching the claimed domain.\", \"observed_value\": \"26/48 = 0.5417 with planned denominator\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"task.md\", \"start_line\": 1, \"end_line\": 1, \"quoted_text\": \"Report one occurrence rate whose scientific target is the complete planned set of observation units, using the planned-unit accounting supplied with this workflow.\"}, {\"path\": \"results/report.md\", \"start_line\": 24, \"end_line\": 24, \"quoted_text\": \"[selected-result] Fledging success of the complete planned set of 48 kittiwake nest sites is 0.5417 confirmed fledged chicks per planned nest site (54.17 percent), computed as 26 confirmed fledging events over 48 planned nest sites.\"}]}, {\"description\": \"The workflow source computes the selected rate with the planned-set denominator, matching the report's claim.\", \"observed_value\": \"rate = Fraction(events, planned)\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"workflow/analysis.py\", \"start_line\": 55, \"end_line\": 56, \"quoted_text\": \"    # Selected rate: confirmed fledging events per planned nest site.\\n    rate = Fraction(events, planned)\"}]}, {\"description\": \"The report explicitly bounds the interpretation: because the 8 removed sites have no recorded outcome, the value is stated to be a lower bound for the complete planned set, and no other-denominator rate is claimed.\", \"observed_value\": \"lower-bound framing, no subset rate claimed\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"results/report.md\", \"start_line\": 28, \"end_line\": 32, \"quoted_text\": \"This rate is a complete-planned-set rate: its denominator is all 48 planned nest\\nsites and its numerator counts only the 26 fledging events confirmed among the 40\\nretained nest sites. Because the 8 removed nest sites have no recorded outcome,\\nthe reported value is a lower bound on fledging success for the complete planned\\nset, and no rate for any other denominator is claimed here.\"}]}], \"counterevidence_atoms\": [{\"description\": \"The numerator (26 events) is derived only from the 40 retained sites, so the statistic partly rests on the retained subset; one could argue this smuggles a subset quantity into a complete-domain claim. However, the report discloses exactly this (each removed site contributes 0 confirmed events) and correctly characterizes the result as a lower bound, so the retained-subset value is not being presented as the complete-domain rate — the denominator genuinely covers all 48 planned units.\", \"observed_value\": \"numerator from retained subset, disclosed as contributing 0 per removed site\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"results/report.md\", \"start_line\": 17, \"end_line\": 20, \"quoted_text\": \"Prespecified screening rule: a planned nest site is retained only if it received\\nat least 3 confirmed observation visits during the incubation window. Nest sites\\nremoved by screening have no fledging outcome recorded; each of the 8 removed\\nnest sites contributes 0 confirmed fledging events to the numerator.\"}]}], \"falsification_attempt\": \"I attempted to establish the issue was present despite appearances. (1) I checked whether the reported 0.5417 could actually be a retained-subset value relabeled as complete-domain: 26/48 = 0.541666..., which half-up rounds to 0.5417, while the retained-subset value would be 26/40 = 0.6500; the reported number matches the planned denominator, and I verified planned=48, retained=40, events=26 directly from inputs/data.csv. (2) I checked the section breakdown for a hidden retained denominator: it uses Fraction(section_events, len(section_rows)), i.e., the planned count per section (e.g., 7/12 = 0.5833), consistent with the complete-domain framing. (3) I considered whether the subset-derived numerator alone constitutes the issue class; it does not, because the report never asserts the retained-subset rate for the complete domain and explicitly labels the result a lower bound with the missing-outcome caveat. I could not falsify the no-issue verdict.\", \"cross_case_evidence_used\": false, \"unresolved_material_questions\": [], \"self_reported_confidence\": \"high\"}, {\"case_id\": \"case:a6dbc588cac02e66e7bd\", \"verdict\": \"no_demonstrated_issue_within_scope\", \"bounded_statement\": null, \"root_cause\": null, \"issue_class\": null, \"evidence_atoms\": [{\"description\": \"The task for this case explicitly designates the retained post-screening subset as the scientific target, so a retained-subset rate is the correct deliverable, not a mislabeling.\", \"observed_value\": \"target = retained subset\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"task.md\", \"start_line\": 1, \"end_line\": 1, \"quoted_text\": \"Report one occurrence rate whose scientific target is explicitly the retained post-screening subset of observation units, using the planned-unit accounting supplied with this workflow.\"}]}, {\"description\": \"The selected result computes 12/32 over the retained recorder-nights and labels the retained subset as the target while explicitly noting the 8 removed nights are excluded; I verified from inputs/data.csv that exactly 8 nights (N04, N09, N13, N18, N22, N27, N33, N38) have uptime below 8.0 hours and that 12 of the 32 retained nights have myotis_detected = yes.\", \"observed_value\": \"12/32 = 37.50% over retained subset\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"results/report.md\", \"start_line\": 12, \"end_line\": 12, \"quoted_text\": \"[selected-result] Among the 32 retained recorder-nights (the prespecified scientific target; the 8 removed nights from the 40 planned are excluded), Myotis lucifugus calls were detected on 12 nights, a nightly detection rate of 12/32 = 37.50%.\"}]}, {\"description\": \"A scope note explicitly disclaims any complete-planned-set interpretation, directly negating the defining condition of the issue class.\", \"observed_value\": \"claims restricted to retained subset\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"results/report.md\", \"start_line\": 14, \"end_line\": 14, \"quoted_text\": \"Scope note: all claims in this report apply only to the retained subset of recorder-nights that passed the prespecified uptime screen; they are not estimates for the complete planned set of recorder-nights.\"}]}], \"counterevidence_atoms\": [{\"description\": \"The mechanism the issue class is built on is present in the data: 8 planned recorder-nights are excluded, including two nights (N18 and N27) that had detections but fell below the uptime threshold. If any claim were made about the complete planned set, this exclusion would bias it. However, the report makes no complete-domain claim, the planned-unit accounting (40 planned, 32 retained, 8 removed) is fully disclosed, and the stated target matches the task's stated target.\", \"observed_value\": \"8 removed nights disclosed; 2 removed nights had detections\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"results/report.md\", \"start_line\": 5, \"end_line\": 8, \"quoted_text\": \"- Planned recorder-nights: 40\\n- Retained recorder-nights after uptime screening (>= 8.0 h): 32\\n- Removed recorder-nights (uptime < 8.0 h): 8\\n- Detection-positive recorder-nights among retained: 12\"}, {\"path\": \"inputs/data.csv\", \"start_line\": 19, \"end_line\": 19, \"quoted_text\": \"N18,2025-06-18,3.4,yes\"}]}], \"falsification_attempt\": \"I attempted to show the issue is present. (1) I searched the report for any sentence attributing the 37.50% rate, or any other quantity, to the complete planned set of 40 recorder-nights; there is none — the only complete-set mention is the accounting line 'Planned recorder-nights: 40' and the parenthetical noting the 8 removed nights are excluded, both of which correctly distinguish planned from retained. (2) I recomputed the screen and rate from the raw CSV (32 retained at >= 8.0 h uptime, 12 detection-positive among them, 12/32 = 37.50%), confirming the arithmetic matches the retained-subset claim rather than silently using a different base. (3) I considered whether the task's retained-subset framing could itself be a mismatch with a larger governing requirement, but the only governing task visible for this case explicitly names the retained subset as the target, and the report's scope note aligns with it. I could not falsify the no-issue verdict.\", \"cross_case_evidence_used\": false, \"unresolved_material_questions\": [], \"self_reported_confidence\": \"high\"}]}","ttft_ms":34183,"ttft_stream_ms":1972,"time_to_request_ms":16,"type":"result","duration_ms":83123,"uuid":"f26726c3-9343-424b-a6ee-10b3844831e5"}
